  "reason": "The reference does not support a single cumulative task time budget across feeds. The Monty resource-limits docs (resource-limits.md L229-246) state there is no cumulative per-session budget: every limit restarts, so a long-lived session is bounded per request rather than over its lifetime (card 265076cf8950). The two duration budgets, max_feed_duration_secs and max_turn_duration_secs, both restart at their respective boundaries (feed and host answer) rather than accumulating (card 265076cf8950). The BrassClaw task account persists consumption and effective settings across steps/waits/retries, but the reference does not describe a single cumulative time budget spanning all feeds (card 9ee64db8b0ee). The removed max_allocations setting must not be reinvented to get around a limit (card 9ee64db8b0ee).",
